
=== Export

Export your configuration at any time through the web console. Open the Configure tab, then click the Details tab. On the Overview screen you there is an [export] button. Use the drop down to select the format you would like to use for the export.


Exporting SymmetricDS configuration might be useful in order to save it in source control or to be used as an import 
into another environment. Export and Import actions are frequently used to migrate configuration between test and production environments. 

NOTE: Group identifiers (node_group_id) are significant in the SymmetricDS configuration. It is a *requirement that Group IDs are identical* in both production and test environments. See the Groups section (below) for details. 

In contrast, server hostnames, database connection strings and other startup parameters are not included in configuration export file at all. 

NOTE: Consider setting the *topbar.system.text*=YOUR_ENVIRONMENT_NAME parameter in the engine properties file to help visually separate environments with identical configuration.
